builtins:
print (s: str)
    stdout, adds `\n`
write (s: str)
    stdout, no newline
eprint (s: str)
    stderr, adds `\n`
read_line () -> result[str]
    one line of stdin without its `\n` (or `\r\n`); `err("eof")` at end of input
read_all () -> str
    the rest of stdin
read_file (path: str) -> result[str]
write_file (path: str, s: str) -> result[void]
    creates or replaces the file
args () -> list[str]
    arguments after `--` in `vo run f.vo -- a b`
exit (code: int)
    ends the program; code 0–63, else R0008
now_ms () -> int
    wall-clock milliseconds; with `--clock-ms N`: N, N+1, ...
random_int (lo: int, hi: int) -> int
    uniform in `lo..hi` inclusive; R0007 if `lo > hi`; fixed by `--seed N`
env (name: str) -> result[str]
    an environment variable; `err("not set")`
str (x: int | float | bool) -> str
    floats keep at most 15 significant digits; `str(1.0)` is `"1.0"`
int (f: float) -> int
    truncates toward zero; R0007 for NaN or out of range
float (i: int) -> float
parse_int (s: str) -> result[int]
    the whole text must be the number: no spaces, no `+` (`trim` first); else `err("invalid int: ...")`
parse_float (s: str) -> result[float]
len (x: str | list[T] | map[K, T]) -> int
    for `str`: bytes, not characters
slice (s: str, a: int, b: int) -> str
    bytes `a` to `b - 1`; R0003 out of range; R0007 if it splits a UTF-8 character
slice (xs: list[T], a: int, b: int) -> list[T]
    a new list; R0003 out of range
find (s: str, sub: str) -> int
    byte offset of the first match, or -1
split (s: str, sep: str) -> list[str]
    `split("a,,b", ",")` is `["a", "", "b"]`; empty `sep` is R0007
join (xs: list[str], sep: str) -> str
trim (s: str) -> str
    removes ASCII whitespace at both ends
chars (s: str) -> list[str]
    one string per code point
upper, lower (s: str) -> str
    ASCII letters only
ord (s: str) -> int
    code point of a one-character string (R0007 otherwise)
chr (i: int) -> str
    the one-character string for a code point
abs (x: int | float) -> int | float
    same type as `x`
min, max (a: C, b: C) -> C
    `C` is `int`, `float` or `str`
push (xs: list[T], v: T)
    appends
pop (xs: list[T]) -> result[T]
    removes the last element; `err("empty")`
sort (xs: list[C])
    in place, ascending, stable
has (m: map[K, T], k: K) -> bool
get_or (m: map[K, T], k: K, default: T) -> T
    the default when the key is missing; never adds it
remove (m: map[K, T], k: K)
    no effect if the key is missing
keys (m: map[K, T]) -> list[K]
    in insertion order
expect (cond: bool)
    only inside `test` (E0410)
expect_eq (actual: T, expected: T)
    only inside `test` (E0410); reports both values
modules:
  std.json JSON values: parse, write, and read fields and elements.
  std.time UTC calendar time, ISO 8601 text and durations in milliseconds.
  std.text Text helpers: search, replace, repeat, pad, lines and words.
  std.random Random floats, picks and shuffles (fixed by --seed).
  std.http HTTP and HTTPS: GET and POST (needs net), and serving plain HTTP requests (needs serve).
  std.collections Operations on the built-in ordered_map, ordered_set, priority_queue and deque.
  std.fs Directories and file information (needs file.read), and file changes (needs file.write, file.delete).
  std.process Running other programs to their end, with no shell (needs process).
  std.math Square roots, powers, logarithms, trigonometry and rounding to int, correctly rounded.
  std.bytes Conversions of binary data with text, integers, hex and base64, and standard input and output as bytes.
